# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# JossPaperAR — environment template
#
# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and fill in real values. NEVER commit `.env`.
#
# Two rules that follow from ADR-001 (Expo/RN + Supabase + hosted AI) and
# ADR-005 (honest client):
#   1. Only variables prefixed EXPO_PUBLIC_ are ever exposed to the app bundle.
#      Anything else travels to the device. Treat every EXPO_PUBLIC_ value as
#      public — no secrets, no AI API keys.
#   2. Supabase service-role keys and AI provider keys live ONLY on the server
#      (Supabase Edge Functions / secrets), never here.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── Supabase (app-facing; anon key is safe to expose, RLS enforces access) ──
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT.supabase.co
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ── Optional: pointing the app at a local dev backend ───────────────────────
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:54321

# ── Server-side ONLY (Edge Functions config — do NOT put these in this file) ─
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=        → supabase secrets set
# AI_API_KEY=                       → supabase secrets set (Path C pipeline, ADR-002)
